# ============================================================
#  Romance sets (world expansion 1, plan §2a): Lyra and Tobias. Each set: spark beats before the confession (two of
#  them repeatable from friendship 9), three partner beats (a tradition, a quarrel in their own voice, a crisis), the
#  ex card (a specialization of soc_ex_encounter), and their versions of generic social cards (`specializes:`).
#  Spark beats need friendship ≥ 9 and no partner or ex bond with them; the confessions themselves are unchanged.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Lyra ----------------

@event lyra_second_place
title: Second Place, Again
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: rel(lyra) >= 9 and courting(lyra) and term
repeat: 4
weight: 10
art: trophy
tags: social romance
scene: A posted list of class rankings on a stone wall, two names at the top, a red-haired girl staring at the second one.
text: The rankings are up. {~Your name is above hers, by one mark. Lyra stands in front of the list with her arms folded. "One mark," she says. "I'll have it back by Frostcall."|Her name is above yours, by one mark, and she's not looking at it. She's looking at you. "One mark," she says. "I'll make it two by Frostcall."|Your names are level. The registrar has had to put you side by side, alphabetically, and she hates it. "A tie," she says, arms folded. "I'll break it by Frostcall."}
> left: "You can try."
  rel lyra +small
  spark lyra +small
  study +tiny
  say: {~Her eyes narrow, and something in them lights. "Oh, I will," she says, and walks off already planning. You find yourself studying harder too, which you suspect was the point.|"Good," she says, with relish. "I'd hate to win against someone who wasn't trying." She's almost smiling.|"Try," she repeats, as if tasting the word. She's in the library before you the next morning. So are you.}
> right: "It's just a list."
  mood +tiny
  rel lyra -tiny
  say: {~"It's never just a list," she says, and for a second she sounds about twelve. Then the Vaneshade face comes back. "But you wouldn't know that."|She looks at you as though you'd said the sun was optional. Then she walks away to study.|"Lucky you," she says, and means something you don't catch until later.}

@event lyra_glove
title: The Glove
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: rel(lyra) >= 9 and spark(lyra) >= 8 and courting(lyra)
weight: 10
art: hand
tags: social romance
scene: A red-haired girl dropping a leather duelling glove at a student's feet in an empty corridor, her chin very high.
text: Lyra drops a glove at your feet in an empty corridor. An actual glove. "Vaneshades settle things properly," she says. "You've been in my head all term. It's insufferable. Dawn, the practice circle. If I win, you stop." She doesn't say stop what. She's gone red to the ears.
> left: Pick it up
  rel lyra +small
  spark lyra +medium
  health -tiny
  say: You meet her at dawn. Neither of you casts a single spell. You stand in the frost and talk for an hour instead, about nothing, and she forgets to win, and so do you.
> right: Hand it back, politely
  rel lyra +tiny
  spark lyra -small
  say: "You dropped this." Her face does something complicated and then goes perfectly smooth. "So I did," she says, and puts it on, and that's the end of it. Almost.

@event lyra_after_hours
title: After the Torches
class: routine
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: rel(lyra) >= 9 and courting(lyra) and spark(lyra) < 40
repeat: 4
time: evening night
weight: 10
art: flame
tags: social romance
scene: An empty practice hall at night, the torches out, a red-haired girl lighting a single flame in her palm so two people can see.
text: {~The duelling hall's torches go out at ten. Lyra lights one flame in her palm and keeps practising.|Lyra is still in the practice hall after the torches are out, working one form over and over.|The torches are out again. Lyra's palm flame is the only light, and she's waiting, as if she knew you'd come.} "You're late," she says. You didn't say you were coming.
> left: Spar with her
  arcana +small
  spark lyra +small
  health -tiny
  say: {~You spar until your arms shake. She says nothing nice, but she shows you, without explaining, how she shapes the turn of a flame. Then she blows it out, and you walk back in the dark, close enough to bump shoulders.|You spar in the light of her hand. She's better than you. She tells you exactly how, and stays until you've fixed it.|You fight until you're both laughing at a missed block. Lyra doesn't laugh, usually. She stops, surprised at herself.}
> right: Make her stop
  rel lyra +small
  study -tiny
  say: {~"Enough," you say, and take her wrist. The flame goes out. "You'll be useless tomorrow." She glares at you in the dark, and then lets you walk her back, which she almost never does.|You sit on the bench and refuse to move until she does. It takes an hour. Your own reading doesn't get done.|You make her eat something. She eats it as if it's an insult, and then eats yours.}

@event lyra_partner_watch
title: Burnout Watch
class: routine
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: bond(lyra) == "partner"
repeat: 4
weight: 12
art: candle
tags: romance
scene: A candlelit desk buried in books, a red-haired girl asleep on her notes, someone gently taking the quill out of her hand.
text: You've an arrangement now, the two of you: at midnight, you go and find her, wherever she is, and make her stop. Tonight it's the library. She's on chapter nine of a book with eleven. {~"Two more," she says, without looking up.|"Ten minutes," she says, which means two hours.}
> left: Make her stop
  spark lyra +small
  study -tiny
  say: {~You close the book on her fingers, gently. She lets you. On the way back she falls asleep against your shoulder, standing up, which you didn't know was possible.|You take the quill. She says something cutting. Then she says thank you, very quietly, as if it costs her a mark.}
> right: Stay and finish it with her
  study +tiny
  health -tiny
  say: {~You pull up a chair and read chapter ten aloud while she takes notes. By two you're both asleep on the table, and the librarian covers you with a cloak.|You stay. She finishes. She says finishing a book with someone there is a different thing entirely.}

@event lyra_not_second
title: Not Second to Anyone
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: bond(lyra) == "partner"
weight: 10
art: flame
tags: romance
scene: A red-haired girl standing very straight in a corridor, eyes bright with anger, a crumpled tournament list in her fist.
text: Lyra has found out you skipped her match for {~a study group|a club meeting|a friend's crisis}. She is very calm, which is worse than shouting. "I have been second to my mother's ambitions my whole life," she says. {~"I won't be second to a study group."|"I won't be second to a club."|"I know it was a crisis. I know. I still wanted you there."}
> left: Talk it through, properly
  hint: She wants to be argued with, not soothed.
  challenge negotiate journeyman:
    win:
      spark lyra +medium
      rel lyra +small
      say: You don't apologise first; you argue. You tell her she's not second, she's the one you'd have fought for a seat beside. She listens. Then she kisses you, angrily, and says next time you'll be in the front row.
    lose:
      spark lyra -small
      rel lyra -small
      say: {~Everything you say sounds like an excuse, because it is.|Everything you say sounds like an excuse, because it is.|You were right to go, and you both know it, and somehow that makes it harder to say.} She nods, very correctly, and walks away. She's at your next lecture. She doesn't sit next to you.
> right: Apologise, and mean it
  spark lyra +tiny
  mood -small
  say: "I'm sorry." She looks at you a long time. "Vaneshades don't accept apologies," she says. "But I'm not a Vaneshade with you." It's forgiveness. It still stings, for both of you.

@event lyra_empty_chair
title: Her Mother's Empty Chair
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: bond(lyra) == "partner" and knows(lyra.mother)
weight: 14
art: duel
tags: romance
scene: A crowded duelling gallery with one empty velvet chair in the front row, a red-haired duellist glancing at it before her bout.
text: Lyra's final bout of the year. In the front row of the gallery is a velvet chair with a card on it: "Reserved — Lady Vaneshade." It stays empty. Lyra looks at it once, just before she bows, and then at you.
> left: Sit in the chair
  spark lyra +medium
  renown -tiny
  say: You walk down to the front and sit in Lady Vaneshade's chair. People stare. Lyra sees, and something in her shoulders lets go. She wins in under a minute. Afterwards she says, "That was a terrible breach of etiquette," and doesn't let go of your hand.
> right: Cheer louder than anyone
  spark lyra +small
  mood +small
  say: You shout her name until the gallery joins in. She doesn't look at the chair again. She wins, and turns, and looks for you, only you, the way she used to look for the scoreboard.

@event lyra_ex
title: Cold Hearth
specializes: soc_ex_encounter
when: seen(lyra_ex) == 0
class: milestone
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: lyra
art: flame
tags: romance
scene: Two people passing in a corridor, one a red-haired girl who keeps her chin high and her eyes forward.
text: Lyra passes you in the corridor with her chin high and her eyes forward. She's perfectly polite now, which is how you know. A Vaneshade's coldest weapon is good manners.
> left: Let her pass
  mood -tiny
  say: She passes. You both keep walking. Behind you, a torch on the wall flares, briefly, as if someone's temper had slipped.
> right: Say her name
  rel lyra +small
  challenge appeal journeyman:
    win:
      bond lyra friend
      say: She stops. Turns. "What," she says. You say you miss her as a rival, at least. She almost laughs. "Library," she says. "Thursday. I'll destroy you." It's an olive branch, the Vaneshade way.
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: "Yes?" she says, and waits, and you don't have the words. "I thought not," she says, not unkindly, and goes.

@event lyra_partner_neglect
title: "I Don't Wait"
specializes: soc_partner_neglect
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: lyra
weight: 14
repeat: 5
art: hourglass
tags: romance
scene: A red-haired girl in a duelling coat standing in a doorway with her arms folded, two cups of cold tea on the table behind her.
text: Lyra is in your doorway with her arms folded. "I don't wait for people," she says. "I've waited for you three times this month. I counted. I'm a Vaneshade; I count everything." She doesn't say she missed you. She doesn't need to.
> left: "Tomorrow. Dawn. I'll be there first."
  spark lyra +small
  health -tiny
  study -tiny
  say: You're there first, at dawn, with two cups of tea that are actually hot. She takes one and says nothing, which from her is an embrace.
> right: "You know what term's like."
  spark lyra -medium
  rel lyra -small
  say: "I do," she says. "I manage." She walks away, perfectly upright. It's the most hurt you've ever seen her look.

@event lyra_lends
title: A Loan, Vaneshade Style
specializes: soc_borrow_money
when: seen(lyra_lends) == 0
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: lyra
weight: 10
art: pouch
tags: social money
scene: A red-haired girl holding out a heavy purse at arm's length, not looking at it, as if it were beneath her notice.
text: Lyra would sooner die than borrow. She has noticed, though, that your purse is thin, and she is holding out hers at arm's length without looking at it. "Take what you need," she says. "Don't thank me. Don't ever mention it."
> left: Take a little
  gold +medium
  rel lyra +small
  mood -tiny
  say: You take a few crowns. She never mentions it again. Neither do you, though you pay her back in study notes she pretends not to read.
> right: Refuse, kindly
  rel lyra +tiny
  say: "I'm fine." She puts the purse away. "Of course you are," she says, and the next day there's a meal paid for at the village inn in your name.

# ---------------- Tobias ----------------

@event tobias_gerald_approves
title: Gerald Approves
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: rel(tobias) >= 9 and courting(tobias)
repeat: 4
weight: 10
art: leaf
tags: social romance
scene: A large gentle student holding a potted mandrake in a tiny knitted hat up to another student's face, both very solemn.
text: Tobias holds Gerald up to your face. Gerald is wearing {~a new hat|his winter hat}. "He's deciding about you," Tobias says seriously. "He doesn't like everyone. He bit the Verdant Circle's treasurer." Gerald considers you with his small dark eyes.
> left: Bow to Gerald
  learn tobias.gerald
  rel tobias +small
  spark tobias +small
  say: {~You bow. Gerald screams very softly, which Tobias says is approval. Tobias looks at you as if you'd done something wonderful. You think maybe you have.|You bow, and Gerald pats your nose with a leaf. Tobias goes pink. "He hardly ever does that," he says. "Not even to me."}
> right: Offer Gerald a finger
  health -tiny
  mood +small
  say: {~Gerald bites it. Tobias is mortified and laughs so hard he has to sit down. You're both still laughing when the greenhouse bell goes.|Gerald bites it, then lets go and looks sorry. "He's shy," says Tobias. Your finger disagrees.}

@event tobias_letter_aloud
title: Read It to Me
class: routine
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: rel(tobias) >= 9 and spark(tobias) >= 5 and courting(tobias)
weight: 10
art: letter
tags: social romance
scene: A large student sitting on a bench handing another a letter on farm paper, his eyes red-rimmed and tired.
text: Tobias has a letter from home and he hasn't opened it. "My eyes are tired," he says, which isn't true. "Would you read it? Out loud?" It's from his mother. She writes the way people talk on farms: weather first, goats second, love last and briefly.
> left: Read it, voices and all
  learn tobias.ma
  spark tobias +small
  rel tobias +small
  say: You read it in his mother's voice, as near as you can guess. He laughs at the goats and goes quiet at the end. "She says she's proud," he says. "She never says that." You read that line twice, because he asks.
> right: Read it plainly, then talk
  rel tobias +small
  mood -tiny
  say: You read it plainly. Then he talks about home for an hour, the farm, the frost, his mother alone at harvest, and you listen. It's a lot to carry. You carry some of it back with you.
  if knows(tobias.after):
    rel tobias +tiny
    say: When he gets to coming home after graduation, you ask what he wants, not what was planned. He doesn't know yet. He says nobody has asked him before.

@event tobias_umbrella
title: One Umbrella
class: routine
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: rel(tobias) >= 9 and courting(tobias) and spark(tobias) < 40
repeat: 4
weight: 10
art: rain
tags: social romance
scene: Two students walking close under one enormous patched umbrella across a rainy castle courtyard, one much bigger than the other.
text: It's pouring, and Tobias has the biggest umbrella you've ever seen: patched, green, and older than both of you. {~"Ma's," he says. "It's seen worse."|"Room for two," he says, "or four, if they're small."}
> left: Walk close under it
  spark tobias +small
  health -tiny
  say: {~You walk back under it, very close, because the umbrella insists, and your outside shoulder is soaked through by the door anyway. He tells you a long story about a goat that fell in a well, and you don't hear the end of it, and don't mind.|Halfway across the courtyard he stops talking. So do you. The rain does the talking, and runs down the back of your neck.}
> right: Race him to the door
  vigor +small
  mood +small
  say: {~You run. He runs after you with the umbrella and arrives soaked anyway, laughing from the belly.|You make it first, drenched. He arrives dry and very pleased with himself.}

@event tobias_seed_month
title: A Seed a Month
class: routine
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: bond(tobias) == "partner"
repeat: 4
weight: 12
art: flower
tags: romance
scene: A large student pressing a single seed into a pot on a windowsill crowded with sprouting pots, another student watching.
text: Tobias gives you one seed a month, every month, in a twist of paper with its name on it. Your windowsill is crowded now. {~This month's is a sunflower. "For when it's grey," he says.|This month's is a herb you've never heard of. "For your cough," he says. You don't have a cough. "Yet," he says.}
> left: Plant it together
  spark tobias +small
  alchemy +tiny
  say: {~You plant it together, his big hands over yours, pressing the soil down gently. He waters it. You'll remember this month by it.|He shows you how deep, how much water, where the light falls. The windowsill is a calendar now.}
> right: Give him one back
  rel tobias +small
  gold -tiny
  say: {~You buy a seed in the village and give it to him in a twist of paper. He holds it as if it were a jewel, and plants it that day.|You give him a seed back. He laughs from the belly and plants it in his best pot.}

@event tobias_home_or_here
title: Home or Here
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: bond(tobias) == "partner" and year >= 2
weight: 10
art: house
tags: romance
scene: A large student sitting on a farm gate in a dream-like vision, then on a castle wall, torn between the two.
text: Tobias has been quiet all week. Finally: "Ma wants me home after. The farm. It's always been the plan." He doesn't look at you. "I always thought I wanted that. I'm sorry. I'm sorry for saying it like this. I'm sorry."
> left: "Then I'll come and see the goats."
  spark tobias +medium
  mood -tiny
  say: He looks up so fast he nearly falls off the wall. "You'd like the goats," he says. "They'd like you." Neither of you knows what comes after. It's enough, for now, that you'd come.
> right: "Do you still want it?"
  rel tobias +small
  spark tobias -tiny
  say: He thinks for a long time, the way he thinks about seeds. "I don't know," he says at last. "I didn't know I was allowed not to know." You sit with him until he stops apologising.

@event tobias_gerald_wilts
title: Gerald Is Ill
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: bond(tobias) == "partner" and knows(tobias.gerald)
weight: 14
art: leaf
tags: romance
scene: A large student cradling a drooping potted mandrake in a knitted hat, sitting on a greenhouse floor, another student kneeling beside him.
text: Gerald is wilting. His hat has slipped, his leaves are grey, and he hasn't screamed in two days. Tobias is sitting on the greenhouse floor holding the pot, and he isn't apologising, which is how you know it's bad.
> left: Brew him a tonic
  challenge brew journeyman:
    win:
      spark tobias +medium
      alchemy +small
      say: You brew all night. At dawn Gerald drinks it, shudders, and screams, loudly, furiously, beautifully. Tobias laughs and cries at once and holds you so hard your ribs creak.
    lose:
      spark tobias +small
      mood -small
      say: The tonic does nothing. But in the morning Gerald is a little greener anyway, maybe because Tobias didn't sleep and neither did you. "It's not your fault," Tobias says. "It's nobody's. You stayed."
> right: Sit with him all night
  spark tobias +small
  health -small
  say: You sit on the greenhouse floor all night, Tobias holding Gerald, you holding Tobias. At dawn Gerald stirs, and screams, very softly. It's the best sound you've ever heard.

@event tobias_ex
title: He Still Waters Your Plant
specializes: soc_ex_encounter
when: seen(tobias_ex) == 0
class: milestone
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: tobias
art: flower
tags: romance
scene: A large student watering a single pot on a windowsill that isn't his, glancing guiltily at the door.
text: You find Tobias at your window, watering the plant on your sill. He jumps. "Sorry," he says. "Sorry. It looked dry. I'll go. I'm sorry."
> left: Let him go
  mood -tiny
  say: He goes. The plant is very well watered. You don't know whether to be grateful or sad, so you're both.
> right: Ask him to stay a minute
  rel tobias +small
  challenge appeal apprentice:
    win:
      bond tobias friend
      say: He stays. You talk about the plant, and then about goats, and it's almost easy. "Friends," he says, at the door, testing the word, "is a good word. I like it."
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: He stays, and stands, and apologises four times, and goes. The plant turns toward the door after him.

@event tobias_dance_specialized
title: The Broom Waltz, Again
specializes: date_dance_lesson
when: seen(tobias_dance_specialized) == 0
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: tobias
weight: 10
art: music
tags: romance
scene: A large student counting steps under his breath in a moonlit greenhouse, guiding another student between rows of plants.
text: Tobias has been practising again, he admits, with the broom. "It complained," he says. "But I'm better now. I think. Will you?" He holds out a hand the size of a spade, very carefully.
> left: Dance with him
  spark tobias +small
  health -tiny
  say: He's better. He steps on your foot only twice, and apologises five times, and between the apologies he's a wonderful dancer, slow and sure, like a tide.
> right: Teach him a new step
  charm +small
  rel tobias +tiny
  say: You teach him a step from the Midwinter Ball. He gets it on the ninth try and is so proud he dances it alone, between the tomato plants, until the gardener throws him out.

@event tobias_friend_sick
title: Too Big for the Bed
specializes: soc_friend_sick
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: tobias
weight: 10
repeat: 8
art: rain
tags: social
scene: A very large student squeezed into a small infirmary bed, feet hanging off the end, a potted mandrake on the bedside table.
text: Tobias has Lake Fever, and the infirmary bed is a foot too short for him. His feet stick out at the end under a blanket. He isn't worried about himself. "Gerald," he croaks. "Who's watering Gerald?"
> left: Send a card, and a promise
  rel tobias +tiny
  say: You send a card with a drawing of Gerald in a sickbed hat. Tobias keeps it propped against the water jug and shows it to Sister Amaranth twice a day.
> right: Water Gerald, and sit with him
  rel tobias +medium
  alignment +tiny
  chance unlikely:
    gain sick
    say: You water Gerald, then sit with Tobias every evening until he's better. Then you're in the next bed. Tobias waters Gerald for both of you, apologising to everyone.
  else:
    say: {~You bring Gerald to the infirmary in his pot. Amaranth objects. Gerald screams at her. Tobias recovers mostly from laughing.|You water Gerald every morning and report on him every evening, leaf by leaf. Tobias gets better, he says, out of relief.|You read him farming almanacs aloud until he falls asleep, which takes four pages. He recovers in three days.}

@event lyra_teach_spell
title: A Trick Worth Learning
specializes: soc_teach_spell
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: lyra
weight: 10
repeat: 8
art: wand
tags: social magic
scene: A duelling hall after hours, a red-haired girl correcting another student's wand arm with two fingers, a scorched practice target behind them.
text: Lyra doesn't invent little spells. "Half-useful is useless," she says. But she'll teach you the flourish her family has used to open a duel for two hundred years, if you swear not to tell anyone she taught it to someone outside the family. She looks as if she might regret the offer.
> left: Learn it her way
  challenge spell apprentice+ likely:
    win:
      arcana +small
      rel lyra +small
      say: She corrects your wrist eleven times. On the twelfth the flourish leaves a ribbon of flame in the air, exactly where it should be. Lyra nods once. "Adequate," she says, which from her is a medal.
    lose:
      health -tiny
      rel lyra +small
      say: The ribbon of flame goes where it shouldn't, which is your sleeve. Lyra puts it out with a flick and doesn't laugh, which is worse. "Again," she says. The second time it works.
> right: Teach her to make toast
  rel lyra +medium
  charm +tiny
  if knows(lyra.toast):
    say: You hand her a slice of bread and a toasting fork. She looks at it the way she looks at a duelling opponent. Four slices are cinders. The fifth is golden. She eats it standing up, in silence, and then says, "Don't tell anyone that either."
  else:
    say: You offer to trade: her flourish for something useful, like toast. She goes very still. "I can incinerate a target at forty paces," she says. "I cannot make toast." By the fifth slice she can. She makes you swear about that too.
